This code uses Jsoup to connect to the given URL, parse the HTML content and extract public classes and methods. It then prints the names of the generated public classes and methods for debugging purposes.

Please note that you need to have Jsoup library in your classpath. You can add it by including the following dependency in your `pom.xml` file (if you're using Maven):

```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.jsoup</groupId>
    <artifactId>jsoup</artifactId>
    <version>1.14.3</version>
</dependency>
```

Or by including it as a dependency in your `build.gradle` file (if you're using Gradle):

```groovy
implementation 'org.jsoup:jsoup:1.14.3'
